  "notes": "Bright QC/Migos-orbit trap built by sample-and-replay, and that method is the whole reason this file looks different from the rest of the bench. Replaying a funk/soul-era source gives \"stronger functional harmony than typical trap\", so `borrowed.V` is raised to 0.3, `seventh` outweighs `triad`, one family resolves through a real dominant (i–VII–VI–V) and another is a plain i–iv–V. More importantly the bass is the *source's* bass line rather than the kick's shadow: `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.6 and `anticipationProb` 0.3, which on this bench only ATL Jacob also does — everyone else mirrors the kick. The transitions are filter and drum-mute rather than fills, so `fillBeforeSection` stays true only for the section seams while `dropOutBeats` runs at 0.7 over four beats. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium and marks the per-track internals [LOW-CONF]: the DAW and credits are confirmed, the drums are not. `kick`, `hihat` and the melodic register are the inferred parameters. ⚠ The i–VI–III–VII and VI–VII–i families are INFERRED — the research says \"real 4-bar progressions\" and names the replayed source but writes no numerals out — and they exist so the generated chord part reaches its distinct-output floor.",
